==Powers and Abilities==
<gallery type="slideshow">
ATG (479).png|Neuroshock Blasts/Levitation
EotB (183).png|Flight/Enhanced Speed
GCBC (219).png|Enhanced Strength/Prehensile Feet
Fame (239).png|Enhanced Durability
ETAtW (218).png|Enhanced Reflexes
PPr (404).png|Enhanced Swimming/Underwater Survivability
TFB1 (245).png|Space Survivability
VoV2 (384).png|Fire/Heat Immunity
THtH (391).png|Radiation Immunity
Fused (97).png|Electricity Immunity
TO (71).png|Prehensile Tail
</gallery>{{Quote|Did you know as Jetray I can shoot out of my eyes AND my tail?|Jetray to [[Oliver Thompson|Oliver]].<ref name="VG"/>}}
Jetray can fire green neuroshock blasts capable of shutting down an organic being's nervous system from his eyes and tail. These blasts are strong enough to blow a hole in a car's engine block,{{Refn|[https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/ben10/images/3/38/AF_Mini_Bible.pdf Alien Force Series Mini Bible]|group = AF Mini Bible|name = bible}} knock down a [[Pyronite (Classic)|Pyronite]]<ref name="ETAtW">''[[Everybody Talks About the Weather]]''</ref> and an [[Amperi (Classic)|Amperi]],<ref name="TRoAE">''[[The Rooters of All Evil]]''</ref> and even cause great discomfort to a [[Vaxasaurian (Classic)|Vaxasaurian]]<ref name="GCBC">''[[Good Copy, Bad Copy]]''</ref> and destroy a [[Sonorosian]] with just one shot.<ref>''[[Absolute Power: Part 2]]''</ref>

Jetray's neuroshock blasts are capable of starting fires with flammable objects, as demonstrated by [[Swift]].<ref name="WXIP1">''[[Weapon XI: Part 1]]''</ref>

Jetray is [[Ben Tennyson (Classic)|Ben]]'s fastest flier; he can fly at speeds several times the speed of sound.{{Refn|group = AF Mini Bible|name = bible}} He can maneuver through the air with little to no flapping and extreme precision, unmatched by anything on [[Earth (Classic)|Earth]];{{Refn|Jetray Plumber Database; files [[:File:Jetray Plumber Database 5.png|1]], [[:File:Jetray Plumber Database Collage 2.png|2]]|group = AF VG}} as well as being able to accelerate to great speeds with ease. Jetray is also fast enough to create sonic booms<ref>''[[What Are Little Girls Made Of?]]''</ref> and enter hyperspace.<ref name="EotB" /> Though, on the ground, Jetray is slower than [[XLR8 (Classic)|XLR8]].{{Refn|[[:File:XLR8 and Jetray Speed.PNG]]|group = DM}}

Jetray has enhanced strength, which was demonstrated by [[Ultimate Ben]] using Jetray's powers, where he was strong enough to catch a fast-moving [[Rustbucket 3]] in midair and ground it before it fell into a cliff.<ref name="B10KR">''[[Ben 10,000 Returns]]</ref>

Jetray is durable enough to withstand multiple blows from [[Vilgax (Classic)|Vilgax]] and gunfire from a fighter jet.<ref name="Fame"/> Jetray is also immune to radiation, as he could withstand a [[Prypiatosian-B]]'s radioactive blasts.<ref name="THtH" /> Additionally, Jetray is also immune to fire and intense heat, such as fire generated by a Pyronite and Vilgax's sword.<ref name="ETAtW" /><ref name="VoVP2">''[[Vengeance of Vilgax: Part 2]]''</ref>

Jetray can safely fly through the [[Earth (Classic)|Earth]]'s atmosphere and into space, and travel on an interstellar level.<ref>''[[The Final Battle: Part 1]]''</ref><ref name="EotB">''[[Eye of the Beholder]]''</ref> Jetray can also breathe and swim fast underwater.<ref>''[[Pier Pressure]]''</ref><ref>''[[The Final Battle: Part 2]]''</ref><ref name="Fused">''[[Fused]]''</ref>

Jetray is immune to electricity, as demonstrated by [[Swift]].<ref name="TRoAE"/> However, Jetray and [[Swift]] have been shown to be potentially hurt by the force of electric attacks.<ref name="Fused" /><ref name="WXIP1" />

Jetray's tail is prehensile, as shown when Jetray carried [[Gwen Tennyson (Classic)|Gwen]] while flying up in the air.<ref>''[[Trade-Off!]]''</ref>

In addition to his tail, Jetray's feet are also prehensile, as he was able to carry a Vaxasaurian in the air with his feet without being tired or weighed down.<ref name="GCBC" />

==Weaknesses==
<gallery type="slideshow">
AF (235).png|Ineffective Neuroshock Blasts
VG (187).png|Neuroshock Blast Vulnerability
WtMH (151).png|Legerdomain Flight Incapability
</gallery>
Jetray's neuroshock blasts are useless against certain mechanical-like species like [[Talpaedan]]s<ref>''[[Andreas' Fault]]''</ref> and robots like [[Computron]]'s [[Computron's Minions|minions]].<ref>''[[Hero Time]]''</ref>

Jetray's neuroshock blasts can hurt himself, as seen when they struck him after being deflected by the [[Stalker]].<ref name="VG">''[[Video Games (Episode)|Video Games]]''</ref>

Jetray can become drowsy if he is hit by quills of a member of [[Argit]]'s [[Argit's Species|species]], as demonstrated by [[Swift]].<ref name="WXIP1" />

Jetray cannot fly in [[Legerdomain]] due to its sky being unparalleled to [[Earth (Classic)|Earth]]'s.<ref>[[Charmcaster (Classic)|Charmcaster]]</ref><ref name="WtMH">''[[Where the Magic Happens]]''</ref>

==History==
===Alien Force===
*Jetray first appeared in ''[[Everybody Talks About the Weather]]'', where he defeated [[Alan Albright|Alan]] and discovered some [[Highbreed Weather Tower|suspicious-looking crop circles]] while fighting with the latter in the air.
*In ''[[All That Glitters]]'', Jetray was defeated by [[Michael Morningstar (Classic)|Michael Morningstar]].
*In ''[[Pier Pressure]]'', Jetray pursued [[Julie Yamamoto|Julie]] who had been taken captive by [[Ship]]. After finding them, Jetray revealed his secret to Julie.
*In ''[[Max Out]]'', Jetray battled some [[DNAlien]]s and destroyed some of their trucks.
*In ''[[What Are Little Girls Made Of?]]'', Jetray was defeated by [[Verdona]].
*In ''[[Paradox]]'', Jetray fought the [[Hugo|Trans-Dimensional Creature]].
*In ''[[Darkstar Rising]]'', Jetray briefly battled Darkstar before turning into [[Humungousaur (Classic)|Humungousaur]].
*In ''[[Good Copy, Bad Copy]]'', Jetray appeared thrice. Firstly, [[Albedo|Negative]] Jetray flew away from a Forever Knight castle. Later, Negative Jetray battled Humungousaur. Lastly, Ben as Jetray fought [[Albedo|Negative]] [[Echo Echo]] but was trapped by Negative [[Spidermonkey (Classic)|Spidermonkey]], forcing Jetray to switch into [[Chromastone (Classic)|Chromastone]].
*In ''[[Save the Last Dance]]'', Jetray briefly appeared before the [[Omnitrix (Original)|Omnitrix]] forcibly changed him straight into [[Big Chill (Classic)|Big Chill]].
*In ''[[Birds of a Feather]]'', Jetray saved [[Lu]] from falling to his death.
*In ''[[Pet Project]]'', Jetray flew to where Gwen, [[Kevin Levin (Classic)|Kevin]], and Julie were.
*In ''[[Inside Man]]'', Jetray battled some DNAliens to get the Oscillator Key, but was unable to destroy it when he decided to rescue [[Tyler]] instead.
*In ''[[War of the Worlds: Part 1]]'', Jetray battled an army of DNAliens before switching into [[Swampfire]].
*In ''[[Vengeance of Vilgax: Part 1]]'', Jetray flew to help Gwen and Kevin fight [[Ssserpent]] before switching into [[Cannonbolt (Classic)|Cannonbolt]].
*In ''[[Vengeance of Vilgax: Part 2]]'', Jetray was defeated by [[Vilgax (Classic)|Vilgax]], so he switched into Big Chill.
*In ''[[Inferno]]'', Jetray destroyed a bomb and escaped the explosion.
*In ''[[Don't Fear the Repo]]'', Jetray battled the [[Vreedle Brothers]] before trying to transform into Humungousaur but transformed into Echo Echo instead.
*In ''[[Simple]]'', Jetray flew down to confront the red troops.
*In ''[[Singlehanded]]'', Jetray escaped some [[Vulpimancer (Classic)|Vulpimancer]]s in the [[Null Void (Classic)|Null Void]] and went to look for [[Max Tennyson (Classic)|Max]]'s old lair.
*In ''[[If All Else Fails]]'', Jetray hyperspace-traveled to [[Augstaka]] (off-screen) to bring [[Reinrassig III]] to [[Earth (Classic)|Earth]]. Later, Jetray flew towards the [[Failsafe]] to get inside of it.
*In ''[[Trade-Off!]]'', Jetray flew with Gwen on a mission to stop the [[Forever Knights]].
*In ''[[The Secret of Chromastone]]'', Jetray fought Vilgax until he reverted.
*In ''[[The Final Battle: Part 1]]'', Jetray destroyed some asteroids, but failed to destroy a giant one, forcing him to retreat to Ship. Later, Jetray flew to [[Albedo]]'s lair.
*In ''[[The Final Battle: Part 2]]'', Jetray escaped from Vilgax and the explosion caused by the [[Chimeran Hammer (Classic)|Chimeran Hammer]].

===Ultimate Alien===
*In ''[[Fame]]'', Jetray was seen on TV. Later, Jetray battled some Air Force planes before saving one of the pilots.
*In ''[[Video Games (Episode)|Video Games]]'', Jetray was scanned by [[Oliver Thompson]] for the [[Stalker]]. Later, Jetray saved a family in a minivan from the Stalker before being defeated by it.
*In ''[[Too Hot to Handle]]'', Jetray saved [[Gwen Tennyson (Classic)|Gwen]] and fought [[P'Andor]] before switching into [[Waterhazard]].
*In ''[[Andreas' Fault]]'', Jetray entered a [[Forever Knights|Forever Knight]] castle, where he encountered [[Argit]] and [[Andreas]] and scanned the latter's DNA.
*In ''[[Fused]]'', Jetray defeated [[Ra'ad]].
*In ''[[Hero Time]]'', Jetray failed to defeat [[Computron]]'s [[Computron's Minions|minions]], so he switched into [[Armodrillo]].
*In ''[[Where the Magic Happens]]'', Jetray tried to fight some [[Rock Monster]]s in [[Legerdomain]], but was unable to fly, so he switched into [[Cannonbolt (Classic)|Cannonbolt]] instead.
*In ''[[The Enemy of My Enemy]]'', Jetray battled [[Ultimate Kevin]] on the [[Rustbucket 3]].
*In ''[[Eye of the Beholder]]'', Jetray went into hyperspace to meet up with Gwen, [[Kevin Levin (Classic)|Kevin]], [[Julie Yamamoto|Julie]], and [[Ship]].
*In ''[[Ben 10,000 Returns]]'', Jetray destroyed the [[Hand of Armageddon]], which resulted in [[Eon]]'s defeat.
*In ''[[It's Not Easy Being Gwen]]'', Jetray went to Gwen's house to get Kevin so the latter could help him fight the [[Mutant Frog]].
*In ''[[The Perfect Girlfriend]]'', Jetray went to fight [[Ssserpent]] only to find his shedded skin instead.
*In ''[[The Mother of All Vreedles]]'', Jetray flew to the Rustbucket 3 to meet with Gwen and Kevin.
*In ''[[Ben 10-Generator Rex: Heroes United|Ben 10/Generator Rex: Heroes United]]'', Jetray appeared as one of the many aliens when [[Ben Tennyson (Classic)|Ben]] was explaining his story to [[Rex Salazar (Generator Rex)|Rex]].
*In ''[[Inspector 13]]'', the [[Ultimatrix (Original)|Ultimatrix]] turned Kevin into Jetray.
*In ''[[The Eggman Cometh]]'', Jetray flew around with the evolution ray on his chest, evolving all of the [[Pterodactyl|pterodactyls]] into normal chickens and unknowingly evolving the [[Sheriff of Bellwood|Bellwood Sheriff]]'s intelligence to superhuman levels.
*In ''[[Couples Retreat]]'', Jetray was defeated by [[Michael Morningstar (Classic)|Darkstar]] twice.

===[[Ultimate Alien Future Timeline|Ultimate Alien Future]]===
*In ''[[Ben 10,000 Returns]]'', [[Ultimate Ben]] used a combination of Jetray's flight and strength to stop the [[Rustbucket 3]] from crash-landing.

