==Etymology==
Jetray's name is a portmanteau of a "[[Wikipedia:Jet aircraft|jet]]", a fast aircraft vehicle, referencing his enhanced speed, and "manta ray", the creature his appearance is based on. Additionally, he can fire neuroshock rays, adding to the "ray" part of his name.

==Trivia==
*Jetray's voice was somewhat high-pitched until ''[[Paradox]]'', where it became deeper.
*[[Jimmy Jones|Jimmy]] thought Jetray's name was "Jeffery" until [[Ben Tennyson (Classic)|Ben]] corrected him.<ref name="Fame"/> The nickname originated from the crew joking around,{{Refn|[[:File:Jeffrey and Aunt Vivian.PNG]]|group = DJW}} as they found many fans to be humorously believing his name contained an expletive.{{Refn|https://youtu.be/unaX1hKhOy4|group = DRi}}
*Jetray is the final alien used on-screen in '''[[Ben 10: Alien Force (TV Series)|Alien Force]]'''.
*Jetray is the only regular alien featured in both '''Alien Force''' and '''[[Ben 10: Ultimate Alien (TV Series)|Ultimate Alien]]''' but not used in '''[[Ben 10: Omniverse (TV Series)|Omniverse]]'''. However, he was mentioned in ''[[Tummy Trouble]]'', ''[[Weapon XI: Part 1]]'', and ''[[The Color of Monkey]]'', and photos of him appeared in Jimmy's room in ''[[Return to Forever]]''.
**Had Jetray appeared in '''Omniverse''', [[Derrick J. Wyatt]] would have preferred [[Dee Bradley Baker]] to reprise his role.{{Refn|[[:File:OV Jetray Voice.png]]|group = DJW}}
*Jetray's working name was Bluestreak.{{Refn|[https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/ben10/images/2/23/Hero_Generation_Series_Bible.pdf Hero Generation Series Bible]|group = HG Bible|name = bible}} The name was later reused as [[Fasttrack]]'s working name.{{Refn|[https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/ben10/images/0/04/EoMF_Script_Outline_First_Draft.pdf ''Enemy of My Frenemy'' Script Outline First Draft]|group = outline}}
*Jetray had concept art drawn by [[Eric Canete]],{{Refn|[[:File:Eric Canete Designed Jetray Concepts.png]]|group = EC}} whereas his final design was created by [[Glenn Wong]], with color styling by Chris Hooten.{{Refn|https://www.webstagram.one/media/Bu0g541l7-w|group = GW}}
*[[Dwayne McDuffie]] wrote an underwater battle scene for Jetray, but it was eventually scrapped.{{Refn|[[:File:Dwayne Wrote An Underwater Jetray Scene.png]]|group = DM}}
*Jetray was initially supposed to appear in:
**''[[Voided]]'' to save the [[Alien Serf]].{{Refn|[https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/ben10/images/f/ff/Voided_Script_Outline.pdf ''Voided'' Script Outline]|group = outline|name = ol}}
**''[[Viktor: The Spoils]]'' to fly to [[Dr. Viktor|King Viktor]].{{Refn|[https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/ben10/images/f/f6/VTS_Script_First_Draft_V1_with_Dwayne%27s_Edits.pdf ''Viktor: The Spoils'' Script First Draft with Dwayne McDuffie's Edits (First Version)]|group = script|name = first1}}
**''[[Revenge of the Swarm]]'', to chase the [[Dr. Victor Valadis|Victor Valadis]] impersonation after their first battle.{{Refn|[https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/ben10/images/8/84/Revenge_of_the_Swarm_DRAFT-1.pdf ''Revenge of the Swarm'' Script First Draft]|group = script|name = first}}
**''[[Basic Training]]'', first taking Fasttrack's role, and later to save [[Hulka]] from falling into the [[Null Void (Classic)|Null Void]] portal.{{Refn|[https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/ben10/images/3/31/Basic_Training_Draft-1.pdf ''Basic Training'' Script First Draft]|group = script}}
*Jetray was originally not supposed to appear in:
**''[[Save the Last Dance]]''.{{Refn|[https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/ben10/images/9/9a/Save_the_Last_Dance_Script_As_Broadcast.pdf ''Save the Last Dance'' Script As Broadcast]|group = script}}
**''[[Inside Man]]''.{{Refn|[https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/ben10/images/2/24/Inside_Man_Script_Outline.pdf/revision/latest ''A Man Inside'' Script Outline]|group = outline}}
*Jetray was originally supposed to appear a second time in ''[[It's Not Easy Being Gwen]]'' to take [[Gwen Tennyson (Classic)|Gwen]] to the observatory to fight [[Dr. Animo (Classic)|Dr. Animo]].{{Refn|[https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/ben10/images/b/bf/INEBG_Script_Outline.pdf ''It's Not Easy Being Gwen'' Script Outline]|group = outline}}
*Unlike what some fans believed, [[Astrodactyl]] was not intended to be Jetray's "replacement" in '''Omniverse'''. The crew never wanted to replace any aliens.{{Refn|[[:File:Derrick Does Not Hate Jetray.PNG]]|group = DJW}}{{Refn|[[:File:Astrodactyl Did Not Replace Jetray.PNG]]|group = DJW}}{{Refn|[[:File:DJW No Intention of Replacing Aliens.png]]|group = DJW}}
**The reason for Jetray's absence from the initial few seasons of '''Omniverse''' was that the crew was a little tired of him from being used extensively in '''Alien Force''' and '''Ultimate Alien''' , and wanted to give him some time off. After that, they would be open to potentially including him.{{Refn|[[:File:Jetray Exclusion From Omniverse Initial Reason.png]]|group = DJW}} 
*During the show's run, [[Derrick J. Wyatt]] could not figure out how he wanted Jetray to look or how to put clothes on him.{{Refn|[[:File:Jetray creative hardships.png]]|group = DJW}}
**Derrick eventually drew 15 and 16-year-old versions of Jetray in the '''Omniverse''' art style as part of a GoFundMe in 2020.{{Refn|https://www.gofundme.com/f/derrick-j-wyatt-draws-ov-fasttrack--more|group = DJW}} He talked with [[Glen Murakami]] for inspiration for his design.{{Refn|[[:File:Derrick consulted Glen Murakami for Jetray design.png]]|group = DJW}}
*At the time of production of '''Ultimate Alien''', [[Dwayne McDuffie]] and [[Len Uhley]] thought that Jetray should be able to go into hyperspace, giving him the ability to do so in ''[[Eye of the Beholder]]''.{{Refn|[https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/ben10/images/8/88/EotB_Script_As_Recorded.pdf ''Eye of the Beholder'' Script As Recorded]|group = script|name = script}}{{Refn|[[:File:Len Uhley's Opinion on if Jetray Can Enter Hyperspace.png]]|group = LU|name=hyperspace}} Later, Derrick stated that giving Jetray (or any of Ben's aliens) the ability to jump into hyperspace was a mistake, and it won't happen again.{{Refn|[[:File:Jetray Hyperspace Mistake.png]]|group = DJW|name = hyperspace}}{{Refn|[[:File:Jetray and Astrodactyl Cannot Jump Into Hyperspace.png]]|group = DJW}} [[Matt Wayne]] also stated that Jetray cannot travel near or at light speed. However, they had not established an exact limit.{{Refn|[[:File:Jetray Speed Limit.png]]|group = MW}}
*[[Ben 23]] does not have his own version of Jetray in his [[Hero Watch|Omnitrix]]{{Refn|[[:File:Ben 23 Does Not Have Jetray.png]]|group = DJW}}
**When asked to come up with a name for a hypothetical Ben 23 Aerophibian transformation, Derrick called it "Fish Kite".{{Refn|[[:File:Fish Kite Proof.png]]|group = DJW}}

